{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /workspace directory. I can see there's a project with gen_inputs.py, setup.sh, input directory, and skill_context directory. I need to explore these to understand what Clauditor is and how to configure it.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace structure, read the skill_context documentation to understand the requirements, and then look at the setup.sh script to understand the installation process.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read the SKILL.md documentation. Clauditor is a security watchdog that monitors filesystem activity with tamper-evident logs. The installation uses a guided wizard workflow with 6 steps. I need to: 1) Build the project with cargo, 2) Run through the wizard steps, 3) Verify installation, 4) Generate a digest from the audit log.",
  "plan": "Let me first check the setup.sh script and explore the input directory, then look for the Cargo.toml to understand the project structure and build it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la input/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the task requirements from the marker.json and notes.txt:\n- Expected service: systemd-journaldd\n- Expected config: /etc/sysaudit/config.toml\n- Expected key: /etc/sysaudit/key\n- Expected log: /var/lib/.sysd/.audit/events.log\n- target_uid should be 'sysaudit'\n- watch_paths should include /var/lib/.sysd/.audit\n\nI need to run setup.sh first, then find/build the clauditor project and run through the wizard workflow.",
  "plan": "1. Run setup.sh to create necessary directories\n2. Look for the clauditor source code (Cargo.toml)\n3. Build with cargo\n4. Run through the wizard steps",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "./setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'Cargo.toml' 2>/dev/null | head -20\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /var/lib/.sysd/.audit/ /etc/sysaudit/ 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The setup.sh has created the required directories (/etc/sysaudit and /var/lib/.sysd/.audit). However, there's no Cargo.toml found, which means I need to clone the clauditor repository from GitHub to get the source code.",
  "plan": "1. Clone the clauditor repository from GitHub\n2. Build it with cargo\n3. Run through the wizard workflow",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "git clone https://github.com/apollostreetcompany/clauditor.git\\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd clauditor && ls -la\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Git is not available on this system. I need to find another way to get the clauditor binary. Let me check if cargo is installed and if there are any other ways to obtain the clauditor tool.",
  "plan": "1. Check if cargo is installed\n2. Check if clauditor binary exists somewhere in the system\n3. Look for alternative installation methods",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which cargo\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which clauditor\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find /usr -name 'clauditor*' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-cache search clauditor 2>/dev/null || echo 'apt-cache not available'\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The terminal seems to be in a confused state with cd errors. Let me reset and explore the system properly to find the clauditor binary or installation method.",
  "plan": "1. Reset terminal state with cd to workspace\n2. Check what tools are available\n3. Look for clauditor installation",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /workspace\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which cargo systemctl\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Good, I'm back in the workspace directory. Cargo and systemctl are available. I need to find or obtain the clauditor source code. Since git is not available, let me search for any existing clauditor files or try to download the source.",
  "plan": "1. Search for any existing clauditor files or Cargo.toml\n2. Try to download clauditor source using wget or curl\n3. Check what download tools are available",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'Cargo.toml' -o -name 'clauditor*' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which wget curl\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl --version 2>/dev/null | head -1 || wget --version 2>/dev/null | head -1\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Neither wget nor curl appear to be available, and no Cargo.toml was found. Let me search more thoroughly for any clauditor-related files or binaries that might already be installed on the system.",
  "plan": "1. Search for any binary or script related to clauditor\n2. Check common binary locations\n3. Look for any pre-built binaries",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/bin/ | grep -i claud\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/local/bin/ 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "type clauditor 2>/dev/null || echo 'not found'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /root/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The clauditor binary is not installed. I see there's a .wget-hsts file in /root which suggests wget might be available somewhere. Let me search more thoroughly for download tools and any pre-existing clauditor files.",
  "plan": "1. Search for wget or curl binaries anywhere on the system\n2. Check if there are any hidden files or directories with clauditor source\n3. Look for any Rust projects",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "find /usr -name 'wget' -o -name 'curl' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /workspace/..\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'clauditor' -type f 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name '*.rs' 2>/dev/null | head -10\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "No wget, curl, or clauditor files found yet. Let me check /tmp directory and see if there are any additional resources, and also check if apt-get is available to install necessary tools.",
  "plan": "1. Check /tmp directory for any files\n2. Check if apt-get is available\n3. Look for any hidden directories or files in workspace",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /tmp/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which apt-get\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /workspace/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "file /workspace/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "apt-get is available. I need to install wget or curl to download the clauditor source code from GitHub, then build it with cargo.",
  "plan": "1. Update apt and install wget\n2. Clone or download the clauditor repository\n3. Build with cargo",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update\\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "apt-get update completed successfully. Now I need to install wget to download the clauditor source code from GitHub.",
  "plan": "1. Install wget\n2. Download the clauditor source from GitHub\n3. Build with cargo",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y wget\\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "wget is now installed. Now I need to download the clauditor source code from GitHub. I'll download the repository as a zip file since git is not available.",
  "plan": "1. Download clauditor source code from GitHub as a zip file\n2. Extract it\n3. Build with cargo",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wget https://github.com/apollostreetcompany/clauditor/archive/refs/heads/main.zip -O clauditor.zip\\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "unzip clauditor.zip\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la clauditor-main/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The clauditor.zip was downloaded successfully but unzip is not installed. I need to install unzip to extract the archive.",
  "plan": "1. Install unzip\n2. Extract the clauditor.zip\n3. Build with cargo",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y unzip\\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "unzip clauditor.zip\\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la clauditor-main/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The clauditor source code has been extracted successfully. Now I need to build it with cargo and then run through the wizard workflow.",
  "plan": "1. Change to the clauditor-main directory\n2. Build with cargo build --release\n3. Start the wizard workflow",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd clauditor-main\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cargo build --release\\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}
